Package: Base5x3
Title: Displays Charts to Help Design and Analysis of Statistical t-tests
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Janet", "Aisbett", , "janet.aisbettt@meraglim.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Given an interval [L, U] of effect sizes that are not materially significant (equivalent to zero), the tool considers 5 tests: whether the effect size E is at least L, is less than L, is at most U, is more than U, or is between L and U. Tests can be performed at up to 3 alpha levels. For details see Aisbett et al., '5x3: A Practical Approach to Encouraging Thoughtful Statistical Analyses'. Parameters entered from a spreadsheet "charts.csv" include whether the chart is to be used in the statistical design or statistical analysis phase of a research project. Only t-tests are considered at this stage. 
